hine learning application so it's  important that we don't just we're not  just running it once we're running it  several times it that we have redundancy  so when another microservice comes along  and says hey R give me some predictions  it's going to first go to load balancer  the load balancer is going to look at  all the replicas of our our machine  learning microservice and it's going to  Route it the one that is free and that  is error free  and then the our microservice will  respond back and then the the full  microservice application can continue  doing its work  and so what's important here as I  mentioned this is a replica set so in  kubernetes  um you have replica sets which basically  says that for this application you're  going to have  um always going to have three instances  of this application in this case  um and if one of the Apple if one of the  replicas goes bad it will be torn down  and a new one will spun up immediately  if we're getting high traffic  we can route new traffic to a free  um replica of our microservice  so it's very important it gives us a  redundancy and it allows us to handle  High request loads this also allows  scaling  so in conclusion I just want to show  that R is great for production with um  proper CI and CD practices continuous  integration up to build and vet your R  practices continuous deployment helps  you release update seamlessly plumber  is an important component for a  microservice because it packages uh your  R code behind an API where any service  that has no knowledge of R can get  results from your R code  and then doctor creates these portable  software packages that you can run on  your laptop you can run in the cloud and  then kubernetes is essentially Orchestra  orchestration engine that will take  those dockerized your doctorized  application and run it in the cloud it  helps you maintain redundancy  um it has health check to help make sure  that your application doesn't  and  yep thank you and uh anyone has some  questions I'd be happy to take them  foreign  [Music]


